Tasks and Datasets. We conduct comprehensive evaluations of HybridAgent on 11 benchmarks across various domains:
(i) Mathematical Reasoning , including AIME 25 ( math-ai, 2025 ) , AIME 26 ( MathArena, 2026 ) , and MATH500 ( HuggingFaceH4, 2023 ) ;
(ii) Knowledge-Intensive Reasoning , including GPQA-Diamond ( Rein et al., 2023 ) , MedQA ( Yang et al., 2024 ) , and MuSiQue ( Trivedi et al., 2022 ) ;
and (iii) Agentic Reasoning , including General AI Assistants (GAIA) ( Mialon et al., 2024 ) , Humanity’s Last Exam (HLE) ( Center for AI Safety et al., 2026 ) , WebWalker ( Wu et al., 2025 ) , SealQA ( Pham et al., 2026 ) , and DeepSearchQA (DSQA) ( Gupta et al., 2026 ) . We adopt the standard evaluation metric for each dataset. Additional benchmark details are in Appendix H.1 .

Baselines. For baseline comparisons, we evaluate HybridAgent against
(i) Text-based Agentic Methods , covering standard text SFT (with tools) and multi-turn tool-integrated RL methods such as GRPO ( Shao et al., 2024 ) and ARPO ( Dong et al., 2025b ) ;
(ii) Latent Reasoning Methods , including SoftThinking ( Zhang et al., 2025 ) , Coconut ( Hao et al., 2024 ) , and SoftCoT ( Xu et al., 2025b ) ;
(iii) Frontier LLM Agents , including GPT-5.6-Luna ( OpenAI, 2026 ) , Kimi-K3 ( Team, 2026 ) , GLM-5.3-Flash ( GLM-5-Team and others, 2026 ) , DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash ( DeepSeek-AI, 2026 ) , QwQ-32B ( Team, 2025 ) ;
and (iv) Agentic Frameworks , including ReAct ( Yao et al., 2023 ) , Search-o1 ( Li et al., 2025a ) , and WebThinker ( Li et al., 2025b ) .
Additional baseline details are provided in Appendix H.2 .

